    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-04T04:10:36+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T04:10:36+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T18:40:36Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T18:40:36Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure ridge over SA will move to the east this morning, as a trough moves over the state during the day, followed by a strong cold front early Saturday. A high pressure system will then move across the state, behind the front, and merge with another high located to the southwest of WA on Sunday to extend a ridge across much of SA into next week. A low pressure system is also expected to move in vicinity of the WA border late Sunday and may extend a trough into far west SA into next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers south of Hawker, high chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of the ranges. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning north to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Daytime maximum temperatures 20 to 27.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 3:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">High chance of showers in the early morning. Mostly sunny day. Winds west to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h increasing to 45 km/h before turning south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-07T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-06T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of morning fog south of Hawker. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light during the morning then becoming southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 3 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-07T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-08T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-06T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-07T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
